           Loading additional Mobile Pages databases
           -----------------------------------------

This file discusses how to load Mobile Pages databases to your Psion and how   
to INSTALL them, thereby making them available to the software.  It assumes 
you have loaded Mobile Pages software, as defined in the file README.1ST

1. Using RCOM or MCLINK
-----------------------
Connect your Psion to your PC in the normal way, starting RCOM or MCLINK
on the PC and setting 'Remote link' to 'On', on the Psion.

Enter PAGESmgr and select 'Download database from PC'.  Answer the simple 
questions and following the file copy, the new database will be available 
for use the next time you enter PAGESi.

2. Using PsiWin
---------------
Identify the 3 letter database code, supplied with the new database(s).
For example, the Expotel UK database has the 3 letter code EXU.

Use Windows based "drag & drop" to copy all files from the \app\pages 
directory, starting with this 3 letter code, to any \app\pages directory
on your Psion.

Use PAGESmgr's 'Database install/remove' option to make the new database
available to PAGESi.

3. REMOVING DATABASES
   ------------------
If you want to stop a database being visible/selectable in the PAGESi
database menu, use PAGESmgr 'Database Install/Remove' and select the
Remove option.  You can make it selectable again at a later date with
the Install option, in the same menu.

If you want to delete all related files for a given database, from your
Psion, select the 'Delete database from Psion' option in PAGESmgr and 
supply the 3 letter database code.  Note that this will delete all 
related Mobile Pages database files from ALL devices on the Psion.
